        "fr-extract.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "68f03beb-0f5c-304c-8399-092ed209ac7a",
                "word": "dolman",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "fr",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "79841547-b342-4539-a586-c5e17dabe944",
                        "entry_id": "68f03beb-0f5c-304c-8399-092ed209ac7a",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "dolmans"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "db3128f4-2e91-3298-9b73-b8087e9403cc",
                        "entry_id": "68f03beb-0f5c-304c-8399-092ed209ac7a",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Veste retenue sur les épaules par un cordon seulement, puis ajustée à la taille et pourvue de brandebourgs que portaient certains corps de cavalerie et d’artillerie, en particulier, les hussards."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "9aff7c48-33ea-401c-a59b-2f5d9c2a5b80",
                                "sense_id": "db3128f4-2e91-3298-9b73-b8087e9403cc",
                                "text": "Le garde-chiourme parlait à une voisine. Son képi à visière carrée, son ceinturon, son dolman noir et son pantalon bleu, à passepoil jonquille, provoquaient dans la rue une grandissante curiosité."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "3809e5a7-0071-449f-9672-18d57b7e0d63",
                                "sense_id": "db3128f4-2e91-3298-9b73-b8087e9403cc",
                                "text": "Le prisonnier, sa veste grise en dolman, car son bras en écharpe ne lui permet pas d’en passer la manche, s’incline avec une expression de joie reconnaissante."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "ac1b315f-2369-4349-83a7-f40392e5d70c",
                                "sense_id": "db3128f4-2e91-3298-9b73-b8087e9403cc",
                                "text": "Le choc des cavaliers français, coiffés de leurs hauts mirlitons rouges, ornés d'une longue flamme de la même couleur, sanglés dans leurs dolmans bleu ciel, contre les dragons anglais aux larges plastrons rouges et aux casques de cuir ornés d’une crinière écarlate, est d’une rare violence."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "1b9eb7ea-5899-39df-a042-f3508282088d",
                        "entry_id": "68f03beb-0f5c-304c-8399-092ed209ac7a",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Vêtement masculin ou féminin ayant la forme d’un dolman."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "broadly"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "abde9089-fc7a-4108-9c81-67e64265c817",
                                "sense_id": "1b9eb7ea-5899-39df-a042-f3508282088d",
                                "text": "Quand Mme Risler sortait […] cinquante paires d’yeux envieux et clairs […] la regardaient passer, voyant jusqu’au fond de sa conscience de coupable à travers son dolman de velours noir et sa cuirasse de jais scintillant."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "dafab08b-dc78-41e7-971b-9d81fa48b4f2",
                                "sense_id": "1b9eb7ea-5899-39df-a042-f3508282088d",
                                "text": "Le joueur de golf se leva pour haranguer le dolman blanc du préposé au wagon-restaurant."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "cd16945e-13bc-4dc2-b654-9a551fc087c1",
                        "source_entry_id": "68f03beb-0f5c-304c-8399-092ed209ac7a",
                        "source_sense_description": "veste",
                        "target_lang_word": "Dolman",
                        "target_lang_code": "de",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "Dolman",
                                "target_lang_code": "de",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "cd92e1d5-819b-3eac-8d20-832d9ead9267",
                                        "entry_id": "afbf939e-e250-33d1-ac3e-c2d5c05e166a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Männerjacke der Husaren"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9ffcb106-fc44-4d56-b495-37c87c172c0c",
                                                "sense_id": "cd92e1d5-819b-3eac-8d20-832d9ead9267",
                                                "text": "„Plötzlich ging ein Platzregen nieder, im Herbst etwas höchst Ungewöhnliches, er knöpfte seinen Dolman auf, blieb, den Kopf in den Nacken gelegt, stehen, trank die Tropfen und fühlte förmlich die von seinem müden Körper aufsteigenden Dämpfe.“"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "516889a4-c13c-49ac-834e-a656f9208c4a",
                                                "sense_id": "cd92e1d5-819b-3eac-8d20-832d9ead9267",
                                                "text": "„Neswitzkij sah sich um und erblickte in einer Entfernung von fünfzehn Schritt, durch die wogende Masse der Infanterie von ihm getrennt, unter dem zerzausten schwarzen Haar das rote Gesicht Waska Denissows, dem die Mütze tief im Genick sass und der Dolman flott von der Schulter hing.“"
                                            }
                                        ],
                                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "34ce9102-2356-314d-8b5c-e725113d426f",
                                        "entry_id": "afbf939e-e250-33d1-ac3e-c2d5c05e166a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "alttürkische als Überwurf dienende Jacke"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [],
                                        "sense_index_json": "\"2\""
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "43f0a844-b3bb-465e-8e48-818ba095f71a",
                        "source_entry_id": "68f03beb-0f5c-304c-8399-092ed209ac7a",
                        "source_sense_description": "veste",
                        "target_lang_word": "dolman",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "dolman",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "d975f52c-13d4-3b99-b6db-3393d21491ab",
                                        "entry_id": "826f9f59-3be2-3a9f-b02f-5fba9bee1428",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A long, loose garment with narrow sleeves and an opening in the front, generally worn by Turks."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6931be0a-9a7d-4b60-a47e-c1efc79f99b9",
                                                "sense_id": "d975f52c-13d4-3b99-b6db-3393d21491ab",
                                                "text": "Feriz Beg, on discarding his dolman, rolled up the sleeves of his fine shirt of Turkish linen to his shoulders, and drew from its sheath his fine Damascus scimitar, which was scarce two inches broad, and so flexible that you could have bent it double in every direction like a watch-spring."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7f733a1c-0ba9-463d-961e-5cd6ab72e49e",
                                                "sense_id": "d975f52c-13d4-3b99-b6db-3393d21491ab",
                                                "text": "[I]n the second half of the century the long Turkish dolman disappears completely and tight, knee-length dolmans and mentes become general."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e7825eae-db23-4cf2-a4b5-83ff0b78aa21",
                                                "sense_id": "d975f52c-13d4-3b99-b6db-3393d21491ab",
                                                "text": "The quintessentially Hungarian item of men's clothing was the dolman. This flowing garment, open in the front, replaced the waistcoat after the Renaissance."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "cf2ea2a7-911e-3b7b-92b1-c6be0729c472",
                                        "entry_id": "826f9f59-3be2-3a9f-b02f-5fba9bee1428",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A short, close-fitting, heavily braided military jacket, usually worn under a pelisse, originally by hussars."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e6ca56d1-505f-4db4-96bb-f797e2817e94",
                                                "sense_id": "cf2ea2a7-911e-3b7b-92b1-c6be0729c472",
                                                "text": "Robert nodded in reply to her question and not only took off his helmet but unhooked his pelisse, threw it on a chair, and unbuttoned the top of his dolman."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "86d43206-291c-4ea5-83c9-40fe6de3383c",
                                                "sense_id": "cf2ea2a7-911e-3b7b-92b1-c6be0729c472",
                                                "text": "Sitting on the chair's edge, he shrugged a shoulder until his dolman fell into place, then balanced his helmet on his knee like a pampered pet."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4d225af9-b79d-4480-9815-5a5b5883a105",
                                                "sense_id": "cf2ea2a7-911e-3b7b-92b1-c6be0729c472",
                                                "text": "He wore his dolman slung over one shoulder and clasped at his throat with a gold chain, and carried his Hussar's bearskin busby under his right arm."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "93c35dc0-f404-4bc3-b27f-154fcc7cc6c4",
                                                "sense_id": "cf2ea2a7-911e-3b7b-92b1-c6be0729c472",
                                                "text": "The uniform jacket with several rows of buttons and a horizontal braid across the front originally worn by the Hussars was also called a dolman."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "fbc63813-1c65-31c0-bd0c-d0939e5220e9",
                                        "entry_id": "826f9f59-3be2-3a9f-b02f-5fba9bee1428",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A woman's garment with wide capelike sleeves."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "157adf36-97e6-4360-a183-6f6c07854646",
                                                "sense_id": "fbc63813-1c65-31c0-bd0c-d0939e5220e9",
                                                "text": "She, who never went out, found a bonnet that I had never seen before, put a dolman over her best silk dress, locked the guinea fowl safe in her kitchen and got into a hack with Henry, her smelling-bottle and her cap, in which was a new bunch of everlasting flowers."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "dc136abe-6907-4d70-a57f-3e602381b1b5",
                                                "sense_id": "fbc63813-1c65-31c0-bd0c-d0939e5220e9",
                                                "text": "She turned slowly – she was dressed in tussore and a dolman."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b17ff539-952c-41bc-b1ca-312224424b3e",
                                                "sense_id": "fbc63813-1c65-31c0-bd0c-d0939e5220e9",
                                                "text": "In general, dolmans are recognizable for their winged kimono-like sleeves and T shape. But the one truism about dolmans is this—there is no standard!"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e3298832-3ae2-4d91-a999-82d5c2cd4a39",
                                                "sense_id": "fbc63813-1c65-31c0-bd0c-d0939e5220e9",
                                                "text": "The dolman mantle, a popular women's fashion in Western Europe and the United States during the 1870s and 1880s, was characterized by loose sling-like sleeves cut with the body of the garment resembling a half jacket, half cape."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
